      "provenance": {
        "notes": "Row 73. NAME CLASH: on Spanish labels 'jazmín' is often Jasminum polyanthum (jazmín chino, row ES9), and false or star jasmine (Trachelospermum, own entry) is a different genus; the matcher turns these into a choose. Toxicity: NC State tags this species non-toxic for cats, dogs and horses; ASPCA lists only the genus (Jasminum species) as non-toxic, which is why it is corroboration, not the main source. No human data fetched, so no child or adult rows. Watering: NC State moist, well-drained, drought tolerant, occasionally dry; RHS moist but well-drained or well-drained; let_top_dry is the agent's mapping, 7 days a guess. Hardiness: RHS H5 (-15 to -10 C); NC State USDA 7b to 10b, not cold tolerant beyond zone 7, can be grown as a container plant and brought in to over-winter; no temperature stored. Size conflict: RHS up to 4 to 8 m by 1.5 to 2.5 m (also 'up to 12 m' in its description); NC State up to 40 ft (12 m) by 15 ft (4.6 m); 6 m by 2 m is the agent's middle. Leaf habit: RHS deciduous; NC State deciduous or semi-evergreen. Es and it names are machine drafts."
      },
